# Shared simulator environment (checked in).
#
# Sourced by bin/build-ios, bin/screenshot-ios, bin/ios-device and bin/test-ios for
# UNICOACH_DESTINATION. A simulator build is
# selected because UNICOACH_DESTINATION contains the substring "Simulator".
# Simulator builds do not sign, so no signing.env / UNICOACH_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is
# required — a contributor without an Apple account can still run a simulator
# compile check.
#
# The backend URL is NOT set here: bin/build-ios derives it from APP_DOMAIN /
# SERVER_PORT in the repo .env / .env.dev, so the simulator reaches a server on
# the same Mac with zero configuration. APP_DOMAIN defaults to localhost, and
# since RFC 156 SERVER_PORT is PER-WORKTREE (derived in .env.dev from this
# checkout's port block, no longer a flat 8080) — so the URL baked here names
# THIS checkout's dev server. A .app built in another worktree therefore carries
# another worktree's port; bin/ios-simulator and bin/screenshot-ios refuse to
# install one, naming both URLs (see ios-app/DEPLOY.md).
#
# `name=` is a MODEL selector, not a device selector (RFC 126). bin/build-ios
# hands the destination to xcodebuild as written, but bin/ios-device — and through
# it bin/screenshot-ios and bin/test-ios — reads `name=` as the simulator MODEL
# and drives THIS CHECKOUT's own per-checkout device, creating it on demand.
# bin/ios-device owns that device's name; see ios-app/DEPLOY.md, "One simulator per
# checkout".
UNICOACH_DESTINATION="platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro"

# A target MAY instead set UNICOACH_BACKEND_URL explicitly to skip derivation;
# bin/build-ios then forwards that URL verbatim (e.g. an externally-terminated
# HTTPS URL with no port). A deploy simulator target sets UNICOACH_DEPLOY instead,
# so the URL derives from .env.prod as https://api.$APP_DOMAIN — see
# ios-app/env/prod-simulator.env (today https://api.uni.coach).

# UNICOACH_CONFIGURATION is optional; bin/build-ios defaults it to Debug.
# Override the pinned simulator name in your own env file if that device model
# is not installed locally (xcrun simctl list devicetypes — bin/ios-device matches
# the model against the device TYPES, not against existing devices).
